      "type": "card",
      "title": "Hoe voel je je?",
      "body": "Six feelings to know cold: *blij* (happy), *boos* (angry), *moe* (tired), *bang* (scared), *zenuwachtig* (nervous), *verdrietig* (sad).",
      "table": {
        "headers": ["Nederlands", "Betekenis"],
        "rows": [
          ["blij", "happy"],
          ["boos", "angry"],
          ["moe", "tired"],
          ["bang", "scared"],
          ["zenuwachtig", "nervous"],
          ["verdrietig", "sad"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "chips",
      "title": "Tap to hear the feelings",
      "items": [
        { "nl": "blij", "en": "happy", "speak": "blij" },
        { "nl": "boos", "en": "angry", "speak": "boos" },
        { "nl": "moe", "en": "tired", "speak": "moe" },
        { "nl": "bang", "en": "scared", "speak": "bang" },
        { "nl": "zenuwachtig", "en": "nervous", "speak": "zenuwachtig" },
        { "nl": "verdrietig", "en": "sad", "speak": "verdrietig" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "card",
      "title": "Zich voelen — feeling as a reflexive verb",
      "body": "**Zich voelen** (to feel) is reflexive — the pronoun changes with the subject, just like *zich wassen* (to wash oneself). *Ik voel me blij* (I feel happy). The reflexive pronoun always matches who's feeling it.",
      "table": {
        "headers": ["Persoon", "Voelen + reflexief"],
        "rows": [
          ["ik", "voel me"],
          ["jij / je", "voelt je"],
          ["hij / zij", "voelt zich"],
          ["wij / we", "voelen ons"],
          ["jullie", "voelen je"],
          ["zij / ze", "voelen zich"]
        ]
      },
      "callout": "*Ik voel me* — say it exactly like that. Not *ik voel* alone."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Complete: 'Zij voelt ___ zenuwachtig.'",
      "options": ["me", "zich", "ons"],
      "correct": 1,
      "explain": "Third person singular (zij/hij) takes zich: zij voelt zich zenuwachtig."
    },
    {
      "type": "contrast",
      "title": "Zijn vs. zich voelen",
      "pairs": [
        {
          "left": "Ik ben blij. — I am happy (simple state).",
          "right": "Ik voel me blij. — I feel happy (zich voelen + adjective).",
          "note": "Ik ben + adjective states a fact; ik voel me + adjective describes how you feel right now — both correct, zich voelen is more personal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "typed",
      "prompt": "Type: 'I feel nervous.'",
      "answers": ["ik voel me zenuwachtig"],
      "hint": "zich voelen, ik-vorm",
      "explain": "Ik voel me zenuwachtig — me matches ik."
    },
    {
      "type": "dictation",
      "prompt": "Listen and type what you hear.",
      "speak": "Ik voel me moe.",
      "answers": ["ik voel me moe"]
    },
